      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should absolutely include those counter-arguments, but you must explicitly label them as the \"individual responsibility\" narrative that ignores the historical context.\nInstead of presenting market trends as the primary cause, frame them as the *consequences* of the initial policy failures that created the unequal starting lines.\nThis approach doesn't just \"balance\" the guide; it teaches students to critically evaluate how historical policy dictates modern market realities rather than accepting the status quo as natural.\nBy doing this, you ensure the curriculum remains factually accurate about the root causes while still addressing the complexities of the present day.",
      "source": "target",
